  "about": "Every model search uses, pinned: the one place to change one (see search/src/vector.rs, 'Changing a model'). Native clients (raft5fs-indexer) and the web app (embedWorker.js, scripts/fetch-models.mjs) read it, and raft5fs-search turns names, sizes and thresholds into its constants when it builds (search/build.rs). The files are raft5fs-embed's: converted from their sources by its `convert` example (the models workflow checks them) and attached to a release (embed/MODELS-NOTICE.txt gives their sources and licences). Each file: its role, where it comes from, its SHA-256 and size, which clients use it, and for the web app the size of the pieces it is cut into (under GitHub Pages' 100 MB a file; 0 for whole). Each model also gives: its vectors' size (dims); the models it replaces, whose vectors devices make again; what goes before a query and a passage; how its vector is pooled (cls, mean); the most tokens it reads; and how search tells a match from a miss (search: floor, margin from the best match, z: how far above the mean of a query's scores, and for text minWords, the fewest words a chunk needs to be embedded), measured as search/src/view.rs says.",
